  "notes": "Original \"6-eye\" deep groove label variation. Unidentified Columbia pressing plant. Runouts are stamped, hashes etched.\n\nThis version:\nSide indicators with full capitalization.\nLarger-sized side indicators (\"1\" and \"2\" are bigger than \"SIDE\").\nOrchestra credit on labels is abbreviated.\nWriting credit for A1 aligned with track title.\n\n\"2\" printed on jacket back bottom corner denotes jacket fabrication by [l=Imperial Paper Box Corp.], of Brooklyn, N.Y.\n\nArtist name appears as \"Miles Davis\" on jacket spine, back and labels.\n\nTrack A2: From ''El Amor Brujo''\n\nPublishers:\nSide I is S. G. A. E. (ASCAP)\nSide II is Gillian Music (BMI)\n\nRecorded 11/20/59 and 03/10-11/60 in New York City. \nLiner notes by Co-Editor of \"The Jazz Review.\"",
  "released_formatted": "18 Jul 1960",
